====== Sinovoip BananaPi BPI-R4 Pro ======

Banana Pi BPI-R4 Pro comes in two variants with separate OpenWrt images:
  * **BPI-R4 Pro 8X** (''bananapi_bpi-r4-pro-8x''): 8 GB RAM, 2x 10G ports (each RJ45 or SFP+)
  * **BPI-R4 Pro 4E** (''bananapi_bpi-r4-pro-4e''): 4 GB RAM, 2.5G combo WAN (RJ45 or SFP)

This page was started from experience with the **8X**. Information about the 4E is welcome.

===== Hardware highlights =====

  * **SoC**: MediaTek MT7988A (Filogic 880: 4x ARM Cortex-A73 @1.8GHz)
  * **MEM**: 8 GB DDR4 (8X), 4 GB (4E)
  * **Storage**:
    * eMMC 8 GB
    * SPI-NAND 256 MB
    * MicroSD slot (shares the controller with eMMC, see [[#boot_media_overlays|boot media overlays]])
    * 2x M.2 Key-M (PCIe 3.0 x1) for NVMe SSD (CN13, CN14)
  * **Network (8X)**:
    * 1x 10G WAN: RJ45 (Aeonsemi AS21010 PHY) **or** SFP+ (selected by overlay)
    * 1x 10G LAN: RJ45 (Aeonsemi AS21010 PHY) **or** SFP+ (selected by overlay)
    * 4x 2.5G RJ45 LAN (MaxLinear MxL86252C switch, DSA driver ''mxl862xx'')
    * 1x 1G RJ45 LAN (MT7988 internal switch)
  * **Wireless**: 2x miniPCIe (PCIe 3.0 x2) for a Wi-Fi 7 NIC such as BPI-R4-NIC-BE14 (MT7996)
  * **Modem**: 3x M.2 Key-B with USB 3.2 for 4G/5G modules; two of them (CN15, CN18) share PCIe with the Key-M slots
  * **Other**: 1x USB 3.2, 1x USB 2.0, USB Type-C debug console, 26-pin header, PWM fan, RTC (PCF8563)

Vendor documentation: https://docs.banana-pi.org/en/BPI-R4_Pro/BananaPi_BPI-R4_Pro

===== OpenWrt support =====

Supported in **SNAPSHOT** (main branch, kernel 6.18) only. Not in 25.12 or older releases, which use kernel 6.12. Support will reach a stable release with the next release branch.

